#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060584} :activity/id #uuid "b1ce0b0f-b6c2-5cc2-9063-1be68a8f54d5" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050136 :topic/id #uuid "2f9e7fe2-15c2-5053-ac76-14e670eead2b" :topic/math-academy-id 244} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060584 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060907 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given two vectors \n$\\mathbf{a} = \\langle 2,3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\langle -4,4 \\rangle,$ shown below. How do we compute the vectors $\\mathbf{a} + \\mathbf{b}$  and  $-5\\mathbf{a}$ in terms of the standard basis $\\mathbf{i},\\mathbf{j}?$\n\n![](images/25/254809cbc834b493759a6fa09222a2c90c5fbfc3280d22e82470e760a7a4c508.png)\n\nTo compute $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b},$ we collect all of the $\\mathbf{i}$'s and $\\mathbf{j}$'s. We know that $\\mathbf{a} = {\\color{red}2}\\mathbf{i} + {\\color{blue}3}\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = {\\color{red}-4}\\mathbf{i} + {\\color{blue}4}\\mathbf{j}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =(2i+3j)+(-4i+4j) \\\\  & =(2+(-4))i+(3+4)j \\\\  & =-2i+7j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our answer in angle bracket and column vector notations, we get \n![](images/ea/eae25a74dde73f7899f6ccbbdbb1a1f589fc72cad9629a33b4fdbbbc753efcd8.svg)\n\nTo compute $-5\\mathbf{a},$ we multiply each of the components by $-5\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot a & =-5(2i+3j) \\\\  & =(-5\\cdot 2)i+(-5\\cdot 3)j \\\\  & =-10i+-15j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our answer in angle bracket and column vector notations, we get \n![](images/05/05f847a73201db3de20db3847ef4ed97e07ea7fae9325401b1ea5a460968f9da.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "84c864c1-dd6f-5d3a-96de-fba662bed5ff" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2914 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "837e91b7-ecc8-5eb1-9d91-ec7da4d94000" :step/math-academy-id 15718 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060585}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060585 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059710 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059523 :question/id #uuid "1d2717f9-b905-59eb-85d7-6db4f9c9dc7f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4292"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63a46dd-b963-5ecc-a96d-e0204ca480a9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048816}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509451} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060392} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060393} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233364} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233365} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509348} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509350} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509352} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509354} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509362} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509365} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509384} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509387} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509400} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509403} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509430} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509432} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509435} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509440} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509449} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573262} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573298}] :knowledge-point/title "Addition and Scalar Multiplication of Vectors in Component Form"} :step/id #uuid "1190044a-3906-5ae4-a51e-538cf356a2c5" :step/math-academy-id 15719 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060586}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060586 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060908 :tutorial/content "To add or subtract vectors given in angle bracket or column vector form, we just need to add or subtract each component separately.\n\nFor example, in angle bracket notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2,5⟩+⟨-3,7⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨2+(-3),5+7⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨-1,12⟩ & ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand in column vector notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+(-3) \\\\ 5+7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, to multiply a vector given in angle bracket or column vector form, we just need to multiply each component separately.\n\nFor example, in angle bracket notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot ⟨2,5⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨(-5)\\cdot 2,(-5)\\cdot 5⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨-10,-25⟩ & ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand in column vector notation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-5)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-5)\\cdot 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -25\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "25665086-90db-5c8c-b344-69f6f45aac54" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2915 :tutorial/title "Sums and Scalar Multiplication of Vectors in Angle Bracket or Column Vector Form"} :step/id #uuid "a19152f2-0fbd-557f-99bc-5538856ff2bf" :step/math-academy-id 15720 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060587}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060587 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059711 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059524 :question/id #uuid "2cb63c87-320a-5cb4-b413-8c6bf9723641" :question/math-academy-id "e-4293"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1735c445-9c97-5aa7-83d6-7dee23993153" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509628} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060025} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060118} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233383} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233442} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509559} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509563} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509574} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509577} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509578} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509585} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509596} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509601} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509622} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509624} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573264} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573284} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573294} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573319}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums and Scalar Multiplication of Vectors Using Angle Bracket Notation"} :step/id #uuid "e88a1726-2670-547f-b2f0-8d69c9477c46" :step/math-academy-id 15721 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060588}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060588 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059712 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059525 :question/id #uuid "43cfef07-255d-5167-b815-267883918993" :question/math-academy-id "e-4294"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a21360f-af5f-5730-85b2-b617de30eaf6" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509557} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060124} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060125} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234272} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234273} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509456} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509457} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509465} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509478} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509482} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509497} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509504} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509512} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509527} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509536} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509544} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509545} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509548} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509551} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509553} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573275} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573312}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums and Scalar Multiplication of Column Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "d24272c4-4b3f-573c-becb-933a5b273063" :step/math-academy-id 15722 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060589}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060589 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060909 :tutorial/content "To denote a vector, we have used two notations:\n\n- a single bold lowercase letter, such as $\\mathbf{v},$ or\n\n- two uppercase letters representing the points of the ends of the vector, with an arrow over them, such as $\\overrightarrow{AB}.$\n\nWe will mostly stick to these notations. However, there are many possible notations for vectors. For example, sometimes a vector can be denoted as\n\n$$\n\\vec{v}, \\quad \\overrightarrow{V}, \\quad v, \\quad \\hat{v}.\n$$\n\nThe rightmost notation, $\\hat{v},$ is usually used to represent unit vectors in particular." :tutorial/id #uuid "25d66dd7-21a2-5d10-a19d-333e279d6e7f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2916 :tutorial/title "Common Notations Used When Describing Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "d6999bc8-a1c0-546d-91dd-6cca922d8030" :step/math-academy-id 15723 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060590}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060590 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059713 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059526 :question/id #uuid "0adf8fad-9a6f-5eb1-970f-11633ba98ca1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4295"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc55e44b-82d0-5145-8a24-d43bc60dc594" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509664} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060028} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060041} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233382} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233395} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509637} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509647} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509648} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509658} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509661} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573293} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573310} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573315}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums and Scalar Multiplication of Vectors Given in Alternative Notation"} :step/id #uuid "75a612c3-28ca-509c-a97e-97bfc17a7e08" :step/math-academy-id 15727}] :activity/title "Addition and Scalar Multiplication of Cartesian Vectors in 2D" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059922}]}
